emfor is a health-check daemon that runs on every application host. It
checks the backends of your services (TCP, HTTP, scripts, and plugins for
redis, MySQL, PostgreSQL and LDAP) and publishes their health in a local
LMDB state store. Applications ask a small client library for a healthy
backend; the answer comes from a local file, so a lookup sends nothing
over the network. An optional DNS server serves programs without a client.
